{"content":[{"c":["HERDSMEN"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Men who cared for domestic animals, such as cattle, sheep and goats (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.13.7-8","r":"Gen.13.7-8","rawR":"Gen.13.7-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.13.7-8","value":"Gen.13.7-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 13:7-8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.26.20","r":"Gen.26.20","rawR":"Gen.26.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.26.20","value":"Gen.26.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"26:20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.21.7","r":"1Sam.21.7","rawR":"1Sam.21.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.21.7","value":"1Sam.21.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 21:7"},"). They also included shepherds. In the NT shepherds were well known. The metaphor of the shepherd and his sheep was used by Jesus (",{"href":"?bref=John.10.1-16","r":"John.10.1-16","rawR":"John.10.1-16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.10.1-16","value":"John.10.1-16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 10:1-16"},"). Some herdsmen kept pigs (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.8.33","r":"Matt.8.33","rawR":"Matt.8.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.8.33","value":"Matt.8.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 8:33"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.5.14","r":"Mark.5.14","rawR":"Mark.5.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.5.14","value":"Mark.5.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 5:14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.8.34","r":"Luke.8.34","rawR":"Luke.8.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.8.34","value":"Luke.8.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 8:34"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Herdsmen","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 13:7-8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.13.7-8","rawQueryValue":"Gen.13.7-8","sourceRefExact":"Gen.13.7-8"},{"anchorText":"26:20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.26.20","rawQueryValue":"Gen.26.20","sourceRefExact":"Gen.26.20"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 21:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstrea